menu "sys_event"

    config SYS_EVENT_MAX_SUBS
        int "Subscriptions (C)"
        default 32
        range 4 255
        help
          Listeners made by C code: inline ones (a device's ON_EVENT) and
          queued ones (the power manager, sys_device_remote; a lane's task).

    config SYS_EVENT_DATA_MAX
        int "Largest payload (bytes)"
        default 64
        range 8 256
        help
          The most bytes of an event's payload (a text of a screen's object).
          A larger payload in an events table fails to compile.

    menu "Lane SYS"

        config SYS_EVENT_SYS_QUEUE_BYTES
            int "Queue (bytes)"
            default 1024
            range 256 16384
            help
              Room of the lane's ring buffer for its events waiting for its
              task (for its queued listeners, its events from ISRs and its
              deferred publishes). An event takes the buffer's 8 B, its own
              4 B, its 20 B header and its payload. A multiple of 4. A full
              buffer drops the event.

        config SYS_EVENT_SYS_TASK_PRIO
            int "Task priority"
            default 7
            range 1 24
            help
              Above the device lane (6), so a flood of device events can't hold
              the system's back; below the urgent task (15).

        config SYS_EVENT_SYS_TASK_STACK
            int "Task stack (bytes)"
            default 4096
            range 3072 32768
            help
              Runs the queued listeners of the system's events (the power
              manager's own, the sessions') and their deferred ones.

    endmenu

    menu "Lane DEVICE"

        config SYS_EVENT_DEVICE_QUEUE_BYTES
            int "Queue (bytes)"
            default 1024
            range 256 16384
            help
              Room of the lane's ring buffer for its events waiting for its
              task (for its queued listeners, its events from ISRs and its
              deferred publishes). An event takes the buffer's 8 B, its own
              4 B, its 20 B header and its payload. A multiple of 4. A full
              buffer drops the event.

        config SYS_EVENT_DEVICE_TASK_PRIO
            int "Task priority"
            default 6
            range 1 24
            help
              Above the router work task (5), below the system lane (7).

        config SYS_EVENT_DEVICE_TASK_STACK
            int "Task stack (bytes)"
            default 4096
            range 3072 32768
            help
              Runs the queued listeners of the devices' events (the power
              manager, sys_device_remote) and every listener of an ISR
              or deferred device event: device ON_EVENT ops (I2C).

    endmenu

endmenu
